  "notes": "Drawn on three open photos of N198NV (left 2024-01 and 2025-03, right 2025-08), two of them fitted to the measured A320 shape. The two sides' fits put the band about 0.02 apart along the body (the left photo is from 14° below); the band is drawn between them. The band is a straight-edged area bent once at the window line (steep below it, shallower above), its purple edging swapping sides as Allegiant's standard yellow edging does. The art behind it is a soft gradient with faint swirl patterns: drawn as four fields, orange, red, magenta and purple, with straight edges where the colors turn; their edges near the crown are the least sure (the titles and the wing hide them). The fin is Allegiant's standard sunburst layout on purple (the standard's rays reused, checked by eye on both sides). The forward fuselage, title and sun are Allegiant's standard. Unveiled before the 2024-01 photo; no press date found, so `from` is left out."
